#: 94379d3306bf4372bb7b74628139a58f
msgid "Towards a theory of quality in documentation"
msgstr ""

#: 643f54426c24424d9900649abe5a57b3
msgid "Diátaxis is an approach to *quality* in documentation."
msgstr ""

#: 04b8e96f638641b7a85eeed806c7c317
msgid "\"Quality\" is a word in danger of losing some of its meaning; it's something we all approve of, but rarely risk trying to describe in any rigorous way. We want quality in our documentation, but much less often specify what exactly we mean by that."
msgstr ""

#: 4dfc1c0d9a0940a0923ee2fccd513b3e
msgid "All the same, we can generally point to examples of \"high-quality documentation\" when asked, and can identify lapses in quality when we see them - and more than that, we often agree when we do. This suggests that we still have a useful grasp on the notion of quality."
msgstr ""

#: 5363a76520314b5fb25425e85af17a20
msgid "As we pursue quality in documentation, it helps to make that grasp surer, by paying some attention to it - here, attempting to refine our grasp by positing a distinction between **functional quality** and **deep quality**."
msgstr ""

#: bf4ad8507a424517a3c8929de036b10c
#: 8e73ad985ba84abf9810f1a3b459d266
msgid "Functional quality"
msgstr ""

#: 68286a068de34efb8e0c0690fa7ff57c
msgid "We need documentation to meet standards of *accuracy*, *completeness*, *consistency*, *usefulness*, *precision* and so on. We can call these aspects of its **functional quality**. Documentation that fails to meet any one of them is failing to perform one of its key functions."
msgstr ""

#: 7a1cb8e1cc6e4b6d9a60b1bf604b03f6
msgid "These properties of functional quality are all independent of each other. Documentation can be accurate without being complete. It can be complete, but inaccurate and inconsistent. It can be accurate, complete, consistent and also useless."
msgstr ""

#: eb5a7815c8e54fef8a139fc1ddbc0d60
msgid "Attaining functional quality means meeting high, objectively-measurable standards in multiple independent dimensions, consistently. It requires discipline and attention to detail, and high levels of technical skill."
msgstr ""

#: 7b1e8e0460284914ba5e6814011f998e
msgid "To make it harder for the creator of documentation, any failure to meet all of these standards is readily apparent to the user."
msgstr ""

#: a6bd763ccd1544b1932f76c5ff93d61a
#: fa1924934a884897b9756c69b8d5e1df
msgid "Deep quality"
msgstr ""

#: 52b239aab2da4eb0947113500ed6741d
msgid "There are other characteristics, that we can call **deep quality**."
msgstr ""

#: 34e9e0885fc24b7bb67fe1fea5388f88
msgid "Functional quality is not enough, or even satisfactory on its own as an ambition. True excellence in documentation implies characteristics of quality that are not included in accuracy, completeness and so on."
msgstr ""

#: 324345453fb146b89855ee2d59c95986
msgid "Think of characteristics such as:"
msgstr ""

#: 2a2b80bcf5b3433eaf739fa013e3a666
msgid "*feeling good to use*"
msgstr ""

#: 1d1d1a8e9b634bdfb42b381dd24a514f
msgid "*having flow*"
msgstr ""

#: ff9d007fb5a04ce989db0990f31aff1d
msgid "*fitting to human needs*"
msgstr ""

#: 7483ac24ef7d4a09988e499c5a7add1c
msgid "*being beautiful*"
msgstr ""

#: 24145975c53a4a65879e835ae5159112
msgid "*anticipating the user*"
msgstr ""

#: 2b9eb208a9e44e138b14bdee42a9239f
msgid "Unlike the characteristics of functional quality, they cannot be checked or measured, but they can still be clearly identified. When we encounter them, we usually (not always, because we need to be capable of it) recognise them."
msgstr ""

#: d9c16a1b2f8f47d9b4dbdbb01515161a
msgid "They are characteristics of *deep quality*."
msgstr ""

#: 2ef18faf250b4934aa28d46367b7f656
msgid "What's the difference?"
msgstr ""

#: ddb016feb2e54ba8a414c805622f3f07
msgid "Aspects of deep quality seem to be genuinely distinct in kind from the characteristics of functional quality."
msgstr ""

#: d00a89a8f1f845d28441edf5d7fc0505
msgid "Documentation can meet all the demands of functional quality, and still fail to exhibit deep quality. There are many examples of documentation that is accurate and consistent (and even very useful) but which is also awkward and unpleasant to use."
msgstr ""

#: 810bcb139a3b4fe0b8d719d51c10e430
msgid "It's also noticeable that while characteristics of functional quality such as completeness and accuracy are **independent** of each other, those of deep quality are hard to disentangle. *Having flow* and *anticipating the user* are aspects of each other - they are **interdependent**. It's hard to see how something could feel good to use without fitting to our needs."
msgstr ""

#: ec74a4469d1f4bdea0d6f50cbe1e7950
msgid "Aspects of functional quality can be measured - literally, with numbers, in some cases (consider completeness). That's clearly not possible with qualities such as *having flow*. Instead, such qualities can only be enquired into, interrogated. Instead of taking **measurements**, we must make **judgements**."
msgstr ""

#: e22742e95f3141a19ae20c9a3b051fe5
msgid "Functional quality is **objective** - it belongs to the world. Accuracy of documentation means the extent to which it conforms to the world it’s trying to describe. Deep quality can’t be ascertained by holding something up to the world. It’s **subjective**, which means that we can assess it only in the light of the needs of the subject of experience, the human."
msgstr ""

#: 3f930b77e697497998992631de9a474b
msgid "And, deep quality is **conditional** upon functional quality. Documentation can be accurate and complete and consistent without being truly excellent - but it will never have deep quality without being accurate and complete and consistent. No user of documentation will experience it as beautiful, if it's inaccurate, or enjoy the way it anticipates their needs if it's inconsistent. The moment we run into such lapses the experience of documentation is tarnished."
msgstr ""

#: fd54745a515943e29d631b754c673b5f
msgid "Finally, all of the characteristics of functional quality appear to us, as documentation creators, as burdens and **constraints**. Each one of them represents a test or challenge we might fail. Or, even if we have met one *now*, we can never rest, because the next release or update means that we'll have to check our work once again, against the thing that it's documenting. Characteristics such as anticipating needs or flow, on the other hand, represent **liberation**, the work of creativity or taste. To attain functional quality in our work, we must *conform* to constraints; to attain deep quality we must *invent*."
msgstr ""

#: f70d6a1dcd174688bd7c229badce9750
msgid "independent characteristics"
msgstr ""

#: f8d45aa353fb46309d88ef0ca4512f0d
msgid "interdependent characteristics"
msgstr ""

#: 0bb6cda757a748a2be8b0677ce6cf862
msgid "objective"
msgstr ""

#: 00d605ef1b734534b6bfe304f388e6a4
msgid "subjective"
msgstr ""

#: b35cf6d164034e0586c78c1ccc6a3a73
msgid "measured against the world"
msgstr ""

#: 30fd79ef10e544179bee50d4f7fedccc
msgid "assessed against the human"
msgstr ""

#: 65c1534e2f5a441b8d6ddf6cc7d1d238
msgid "a condition of deep quality"
msgstr ""

#: 2694934545484c359b73e48a71ca869b
msgid "conditional upon functional quality"
msgstr ""

#: 135ad7616f4f497fa9a65f6de71e6c4c
msgid "aspects of constraint"
msgstr ""

#: b064900db9da40c4bb53c0516b221211
msgid "aspects of liberation"
msgstr ""

#: beb08e432dcb4392bd9feb635c53a1dc
msgid "How we recognise deep quality"
msgstr ""

#: cc86af0bb0ff4c70bb31ec9bd60920a6
msgid "Consider how we judge the quality of say, clothing. Clothes must have *functional quality* (they must keep us appropriately warm and dry, stand up to wear). These things are objectively measurable. You don't really need to know much about clothes to assess how well they do those things. If water gets in, or the clothing falls apart - it lacks quality."
msgstr ""

#: 38902f7066a14ef39e740f8aee69b1eb
msgid "There are other characteristics of quality in clothing that can't simply be measured objectively, and to recognise those characteristics, we need to have an understanding of clothing. The quality of materials or workmanship isn't always immediately obvious. Being able to judge that an item of clothing hangs well, moves well or has been expertly shaped requires developing at least a basic eye for those things. And these are its characteristics of *deep quality*."
msgstr ""

#: 0c21bd2d7b604161b669c6b2892a9836
msgid "But: even someone who can't recognise, or fails to understand, those characteristics - who cannot say *what* they are - can still recognise very well *that* the clothing is excellent, because they find it that **it feels good to wear**, because it's such that they want to wear it. No expertise is required to realise that clothing does or doesn't feel comfortable as you move in it, that it fits and moves with you well. *Your body knows it*."
msgstr ""

#: f0fd468ed4c9458b89e2641b271edb8b
msgid "And it's the same in documentation. Perhaps you need to be a connoisseur to recognise *what* it is that makes some documentation excellent, but that's not necessary to be able to realise *that* it is excellent. Good documentation **feels good**; you feel pleasure and satisfaction when you use it - it feels like it fits and moves with you."
msgstr ""

#: 4f76908b84e949d480bdc8dc112162ad
msgid "The users of our documentation may or may not have the understanding to say why it's good, or where its quality lapses. They might recognise only the more obvious aspects of functional quality in it, mistaking those for its deeper excellence. That doesn't matter - it will feel good, or not, and that's what is important."
msgstr ""

#: 82495e135bbe4ecdaa01e854803be412
msgid "But we, as its creators, need a clear and effective understanding of what makes documentation good. We need to develop our sense of it so that we recognise *what* is good about it, as well as *that* it is good. And we need to develop an understanding of how people will *feel* when they're using it."
msgstr ""

#: 5b083b393d484438b5704f9886bae40f
msgid "Producing work of deep quality depends on our ability to do this."
msgstr ""

#: 78f8635918544557b4fdc33e7b465e02
msgid "Diátaxis and quality"
msgstr ""

#: fb26f84aead2403ea85cafd43ddd153d
msgid "Functional quality's obligations are met through conscientious observance of the demands of the craft of documentation. They require solid skill and knowledge of the technical domain, the ability to gather up a complete terrain into a single, coherent, consistent map of it."
msgstr ""

#: 59257bfad75d4d30ad37b35141deaa67
msgid "**Diátaxis cannot address functional quality in documentation.** It is concerned only with certain aspects of deep quality, some more than others - though if all the aspects of deep quality are tangled up in each other, then it affects all of them."
msgstr ""

#: 3a16786b04004a1491bdc2147b008c48
msgid "Exposing lapses in functional quality"
msgstr ""

#: 32c1cf2205fe48e7930d092ce625df3c
msgid "Although Diátaxis cannot address, or *give* us, functional quality, it can still serve it."
msgstr ""

#: 69a7038995dd4649a6970381f16596db
msgid "It works very effectively to *expose* lapses in functional quality. It's often remarked that one effect of applying Diátaxis to existing documentation is that problems in it suddenly become apparent that were obscured before."
msgstr ""

#: 8ee30d994491498c9e16af308fdfa8ba
msgid "For example: the Diátaxis approach recommends that :ref:`the architecture of reference documentation should reflect the architecture of the code it documents <respect-structure>`. This makes gaps in the documentation much more clearly visible."
msgstr ""

#: a1e47ca7714d4918b0e8e0ed0b2ea9ea
msgid "Or, moving explanatory verbiage out of a tutorial (in accordance with Diátaxis demands) often has the effect of highlighting a section where the reader has been left to work something out for themselves."
msgstr ""

#: 8ae7141bcebe49bbb90a6ec377d1724c
msgid "But, as far as functional quality goes, Diátaxis principles can have only an *analytical* role."
msgstr ""

#: 892827557e914a6a9710b9adb57b280d
msgid "Creating deep quality"
msgstr ""

#: b35eb662cce347559c28a75f7136dd35
msgid "In deep quality on the other hand, the Diátaxis approach can do more."
msgstr ""

#: 018203a11b6e4464a98874d4d5b9e65c
msgid "For example, it helps documentation *fit user needs* by describing documentation modes that are based on them; its categories exist as a response to needs."
msgstr ""

#: dff9b932e73e4afc95082a0798c5d801
msgid "We must pay attention to the correct organisation of these categories then, and the arrangement of its material and the relationships within them, the form and language adopted in different parts of documentation - as a way of fitting to user needs."
msgstr ""

#: a21b4059e1ff47129f6d863734f8bde6
msgid "Or, in Diátaxis we are directly concerned with *flow*. In flow - whether the context is documentation or anything else - we experience a movement from one stage or state to another that seems right, unforced and in sympathy with both our concerns of the moment, and the way our minds and bodies work in general."
msgstr ""

#: ef23f7aad64c475db4f88ee4c50ec410
msgid "Diátaxis preserves flow by helping prevent the kind of disruption of rhythm that occurs when something runs across our purpose and steady progress towards it (for example when a digression into explanation interrupts a how-to guide)."
msgstr ""

#: eb474239a1fb42f2a1eefd9446ad2a44
msgid "And so on."
msgstr ""

#: 96a7cd59f085474bbbf989a9b5a8c1aa
msgid "Understanding the limits"
msgstr ""

#: 1a3d736c86b3416f9d9f6ac152d4c1a6
msgid "It's important to understand that Diátaxis can never be *all* that is required in the pursuit of deep quality."
msgstr ""

#: 1aab434105b54bbdb2f4299f32c240fc
msgid "For example, while it can *help* attain beauty in documentation, at least in its overall form, it doesn't by itself *make documentation beautiful*."
msgstr ""

#: aff71a34fd0b4a75a3431e401cff46aa
msgid "Diátaxis offers a set of principles - it doesn't offer a formula. It certainly cannot offer a short-cut to success, bypassing the skills and insights of disciplines such as user experience or user interaction design, or even visual design."
msgstr ""

#: 91ad9bbd83044b9eae94ca3032069c6c
msgid "Using Diátaxis does not guarantee deep quality. The characteristics of deep quality are forever being renegotiated, reinterpreted, rediscovered and reinvented. But what Diátaxis *can* do is lay down some conditions for the *possibility* of deep quality in documentation."
msgstr ""
